				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Add missing diagnostic log for unmatched revealRange URI\n\nComplete the diagnostic logging added in the full-URI matching fix by emitting a \\`[SkyBridge] editor/revealRange: no editor matches <URI>\\` diagnostic when revealRange fails to resolve an editor. This operation was left without a logging path when the Matched tracking was introduced for the other editor operations, depriving operators of visibility into stale or mismatched URIs for scroll-reveal commands.",
			"SHA": "896cf7258e7e08897d6f7f7c642c007f46287070"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:38:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				5
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Enforce full-URI editor matching to prevent cross-editor bleed\n\nReplace suffix-based editor lookup (`endsWith`) with strict full-URI equality in three SkyBridge operations — decoration set-ranges, text edits, and scroll-position. The suffix match caused commands targeting one file (e.g. `src/foo/index.ts`) to bleed into every other editor whose model shared the same basename (`src/bar/index.ts`, `test/index.ts`), resulting in misplaced decorations, applied edits, and scroll jumps across unrelated tabs.\n\nAlongside this core fix:\n- Correct the model service fallback in InstallEditorAndOutput from `ModelService` to `Models`.\n- Add `Matched` tracking with diagnostic logging via `MountainIPCInvoke` when no editor resolves, giving operators visibility into stale or mismatched URIs.\n- Refactor ProbeServices to use the `ToMountain` wrapper instead of raw `invoke(\"MountainIPCInvoke\", ...)` plus try/catch — reducing boilerplate and centralizing IPC calls.\n- Update Architecture.md and DeepDive.md: fix repository/issue links to point to the Land monorepo, correct opening descriptions, and add the standard maintainer footer to DeepDive.\n\nEditor operations now reliably target the intended editor by exact URI, and unmatched commands produce actionable diagnostics instead of silently affecting the wrong view.",
			"SHA": "53afb5281516509009a741209f8eace64a9916fc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:23:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Expand README with architecture details and consistent formatting\n\nRestructure the README with comprehensive new sections covering Key Features, Core Architecture Principles, Workbench Variants, and System Architecture connection paths. Add expanded Key Components and Project Structure trees with deeper path annotations. Include a new \"In the Land Project\" role table and a PlayForm stewardship note under Funding.\n\nFormatting changes: apply em-quad (U+2001) spacing in section headings consistently per CodeEditorLand convention, standardize table styling with left-aligned headers, wrap prose at 80-100 characters throughout, and add a prominent architecture quote as a tagline. Add the Mountain repository link to Related Documentation.\n\nThis makes the README a more complete technical reference for the Sky UI component layer, documenting its multi-variant workbench system, SkyBridge event routing, and build pipeline integration.",
			"SHA": "94429a7c9723f8a7cf46fbe18de0e858e1455615"
